│ patch_description        │ Replace the fixed exponentially weighted average with a causal robust alpha-beta tracker. │
│                          │ Unlike a window average, this predictor explicitly estimates both level and slope, so its │
│                          │ one-sample prediction compensates filtering lag. Innovation magnitude is measured against │
│                          │ a rolling MAD noise estimate; large isolated deviations are clipped rather than allowed   │
│                          │ to create spurious direction changes. Gains increase only for persistent, statistically   │
│                          │ significant innovations, preserving responsiveness during genuine moves while retaining   │
│                          │ strong smoothing in noisy periods. A slope deadband suppresses low-amplitude sign flips   │
│                          │ that are likely noise-induced reversals. The returned samples remain aligned to the       │
│                          │ trailing endpoint of each window, preserving the current public output-length and         │
│                          │ alignment contract.                                                                       │
