│ patch_description        │ Replace the fixed exponential moving average with a causal, robust local-trend Kalman     │
│                          │ filter. The filter tracks both signal level and slope, which substantially reduces the    │
│                          │ lag inherent in a sliding weighted average while retaining smoothing. Its                 │
│                          │ measurement-noise estimate adapts from recent innovations, allowing it to become more     │
│                          │ conservative during volatile/noisy periods and more responsive when observations become   │
│                          │ consistent.                                                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Innovation clipping prevents isolated spikes from causing large level or slope            │
│                          │ corrections, directly reducing noise-induced directional reversals. The output remains    │
│                          │ causally aligned to the newest sample of each window, preserving the existing output      │
│                          │ length and downstream alignment contract.                                                 │
