│ patch_name               │ hysteretic_slope_reversal                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Add a short confirmation hysteresis for slope sign changes. The current alpha-beta        │
│                          │ tracker can reverse its slope estimate from a single noisy innovation, which explains the │
│                          │ elevated slope-change and false-reversal counts despite good tracking accuracy. The       │
│                          │ replacement requires two consecutive, noise-significant slope proposals in the new        │
│                          │ direction before accepting a reversal. While confirmation is pending, the existing slope  │
│                          │ is only gently decayed, preventing noise-driven direction flips while retaining rapid     │
│                          │ acceptance of sustained genuine turns. The normal same-direction update is unchanged in   │
│                          │ character, preserving responsiveness and low latency.                                     │
