│ patch_name               │ robust_trend_compensation                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the lagging exponential moving average with a robust, weighted local-linear       │
│                          │ endpoint estimator. Each trailing window estimates its local slope using exponentially    │
│                          │ weighted regression, clips large residuals with a Huber-style reweighting pass, and       │
│                          │ applies only a bounded fraction of the inferred trend correction to the weighted level    │
│                          │ estimate. This substantially reduces moving-average phase lag while retaining smoothing.  │
│                          │ The robust residual pass prevents isolated spikes from biasing the slope and causing      │
│                          │ false reversals; the final light causal continuity blend further suppresses short         │
│                          │ one-sample directional changes without adding meaningful latency.                         │
