│ patch_name               │ hysteretic_trend_tracker                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Stabilize the causal alpha-beta tracker with two complementary changes. First, bootstrap  │
│                          │ the robust innovation scale from recent measurement differences during the first few      │
│                          │ samples; this avoids the near-zero initial MAD causing excessive innovation clipping and  │
│                          │ delayed tracker acquisition. Second, replace the instantaneous slope sign crossing logic  │
│                          │ with significance-gated two-sample reversal confirmation. Small or isolated counter-trend │
│                          │ innovations are damped rather than immediately changing the prediction direction,         │
│                          │ reducing slope changes and false reversals. Confirmed directional moves retain a stronger │
│                          │ slope update to limit turning-point lag.                                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 3                                                                                         │
