│ patch_description        │ This approach replaces the state-space Kalman tracker with a causal multi-scale robust    │
│                          │ local-polynomial estimator. For every endpoint, it fits robust quadratic trends over both │
│                          │ short and long trailing windows, then adaptively blends them according to slope agreement │
│                          │ and residual noise. The short fit preserves rapid genuine dynamics, while the longer fit  │
│                          │ suppresses volatile noise. A directional hysteresis layer requires weak slope reversals   │
│                          │ to persist before accepting them, reducing noise-induced reversals without adding the     │
│                          │ phase delay of a moving average. The result remains causal, emits one value per completed │
│                          │ window, and preserves the original API and output alignment.                              │
