│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ persistent_reversal_gate                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Add a causal persistence gate to the predictive continuity stage. The robust local fit    │
│                          │ already supplies a MAD-derived residual scale, but the output can still reverse direction │
│                          │ when a single noisy window shifts the candidate estimate across the previous trajectory.  │
│                          │ The new gate only intervenes when a proposed output velocity opposes the established      │
│                          │ direction: a normal reversal must persist for two consecutive windows, while a large      │
│                          │ movement (at least 0.45 times the local robust scale) is accepted immediately. Holding    │
│                          │ one ambiguous sample avoids noise-induced directional flips with only a one-sample        │
│                          │ bounded delay for genuine sustained turns. The accepted velocity, rather than the raw     │
│                          │ candidate velocity, updates the predictor state so rejected reversals cannot contaminate  │
│                          │ later predictions.                                                                        │
