│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ trend_consistency_gain_gate                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Add a short-horizon versus full-window slope-consistency gate to the adaptive tracker.    │
│                          │ The current Kalman correction can respond strongly to a locally noisy innovation even     │
│                          │ when the recent direction disagrees with the broader trend, contributing to its           │
│                          │ relatively high slope-change and false-reversal counts. The new statistic computes        │
│                          │ inexpensive least-squares slopes over the retained measurement window and its newest 6–10 │
│                          │ samples. Process noise and measurement gain are restricted when the slopes disagree or    │
│                          │ have substantially incompatible magnitudes. Coherent sustained motion still retains the   │
│                          │ normal high-gain response, while isolated turns are smoothed until they gain multi-sample │
│                          │ support. This directly trades a small amount of impulsive responsiveness for improved     │
│                          │ smoothness and reversal reliability without adding phase delay or changing the public     │
│                          │ API.                                                                                      │
│ num_applied              │ 4                                                                                         │
