│ patch_name               │ retune_robust_tracker                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Retune the endpoint tracker toward a slightly longer recency scale and less aggressive    │
│                          │ maximum state correction. The current tracker is highly responsive but residual false     │
│                          │ reversals remain, indicating that transient endpoint-fit errors can still produce overly  │
│                          │ large state changes. Increasing the exponential history from -2.5 to -2.85 improves local │
│                          │ slope stability without introducing moving-average phase lag, because the fitted          │
│                          │ intercept remains endpoint aligned. Centering the residual MAD prevents a biased local    │
│                          │ line residual distribution from overstating or understating the adaptive noise scale.     │
│                          │ Finally, bounding the innovation used for both level and velocity updates limits isolated │
│                          │ excursions while preserving strong responsiveness through activity-dependent gains. The   │
│                          │ revised maximum alpha gain is 0.68, within the recommended 0.65–0.72 range.               │
