│ patch_name               │ robust_trend_gated_tracker                                                                │
│ patch_description        │ The current implementation uses an adaptive alpha-beta tracker with alpha values of       │
│                          │ 0.24–0.52, beta values of 0.035–0.105, a 3-sigma innovation clip, and only a small `0.12  │
│                          │ * noise_scale` slope deadband. This produces good correlation and lag, but the gain can   │
│                          │ become high even when recent directional evidence is inconsistent, resulting in excessive │
│                          │ slope changes and false reversals.                                                        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new implementation combines a robust causal alpha-beta tracker with a                 │
│                          │ short-horizon/full-window trend-consistency gate. It estimates slopes using weighted      │
│                          │ local linear regression over both the full window and a recent subwindow. High gains are  │
│                          │ enabled only when both slope estimates agree in direction and have comparable magnitude.  │
│                          │ Otherwise, level gain is capped near 0.38 and velocity gain near 0.045. Reversals         │
│                          │ additionally require two consecutive significant, coherent counter-trend observations. A  │
│                          │ rolling MAD estimate based on first differences provides stable noise-scale bootstrap and │
│                          │ robust innovation clipping. This reduces noise-induced direction changes while preserving │
│                          │ responsive tracking during genuine trend transitions.                                     │
