│ patch_name               │ robust_multiscale_loess                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This replaces recursive Kalman state updates with a causal, robust, multi-scale           │
│                          │ local-polynomial estimator. At every endpoint it fits weighted quadratic models over both │
│                          │ short and long trailing histories, using Tukey/Huber-style robust reweighting to reject   │
│                          │ spikes. The two estimates are adaptively blended: the short model dominates during        │
│                          │ genuine high-curvature motion, while the longer model suppresses noise during stable      │
│                          │ regions. A noise-scaled directional hysteresis stage then rejects tiny opposite-direction │
│                          │ movements without delaying meaningful reversals. This directly targets false reversals    │
│                          │ and slope-change reduction while retaining endpoint alignment and low-lag trend tracking. │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
