│ patch_name               │ asymmetric_endpoint_robustness                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ Add a one-pass robust reweighting step to the causal quadratic endpoint fit. The initial  │
│                          │ fit still captures genuine local curvature, then residual-based Huber weights limit       │
│                          │ leverage from impulsive samples. When the newest samples oppose both the fitted local     │
│                          │ slope and the tracker velocity, they receive a tighter clipping threshold. This           │
│                          │ specifically prevents isolated endpoint spikes from producing large innovations and false │
│                          │ direction changes, while sustained reversals retain influence because multiple coherent   │
│                          │ counter-trend samples are not all rejected. The additional matrix solve is only 3x3 per   │
│                          │ window and keeps latency low.                                                             │
