│ patch_description        │ This crossover retains the current program’s endpoint-aligned weighted quadratic          │
│                          │ observation model, which provides strong tracking accuracy and low lag, while             │
│                          │ incorporating the inspiration program’s robust difference-MAD noise floor, persistent     │
│                          │ trend confirmation, and direction-stable output handling.                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The implementation uses a short causal quadratic fit to estimate the current endpoint and │
│                          │ local slope, an adaptive alpha-beta state update for responsiveness, and two-horizon      │
│                          │ slope agreement to distinguish genuine directional movement from local noise. Reversals   │
│                          │ require persistent, statistically meaningful counter-trend evidence. The presentation     │
│                          │ output applies a limited monotonic constraint only while a direction is confirmed,        │
│                          │ preventing small noise-induced output reversals without freezing the internal tracker or  │
│                          │ substantially increasing lag. Baseline moving-average computation is also vectorized for  │
│                          │ efficiency.                                                                               │
