│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ broader_regression_kernel                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Broaden the exponential regression kernel so the endpoint polynomial is estimated from a  │
│                          │ slightly longer effective history. The previous newest-to-oldest weighting ratio is       │
│                          │ aggressively concentrated at the newest observations, which allows short noise bursts to  │
│                          │ alter the fitted slope and subsequently create false reversals. Reducing the decay from   │
│                          │ 2.7 to 2.3 gives recent samples dominant influence while increasing support from adjacent │
│                          │ history. The alpha-beta measurement gain is modestly capped at 0.60 to prevent the state  │
│                          │ position from immediately following residual endpoint noise; the endpoint-aligned         │
│                          │ quadratic fit and velocity prediction retain responsiveness without introducing           │
│                          │ moving-average phase delay.                                                               │
