╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ gated_multiscale_tracker                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ The previous endpoint-regression approach used short-model weights up to 0.70 and only a  │
│                          │ very small reversal deadband (0.11× local scale), which retained responsiveness but       │
│                          │ allowed many noise-driven slope changes and false reversals. This version retains robust  │
│                          │ short/long endpoint fits, but replaces direct output emission with a causal alpha-beta    │
│                          │ trend tracker.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Uses two robust IRLS local-linear fits with a shorter horizon of 45% of the window      │
│                          │ rather than 52%, reducing short-window noise sensitivity.                                 │
│                          │ - Uses slope-coherence weighting in the range 0.30–0.64, favoring the stable long model   │
│                          │ when local slopes disagree.                                                               │
│                          │ - Adds innovation-consistency gating: endpoint innovations opposing both prior velocity   │
│                          │ and fitted slope have measurement gain capped at 0.38 and are bounded to 1.8 noise        │
│                          │ scales.                                                                                   │
│                          │ - Uses adaptive position gain (0.24–0.60) and velocity learning rate (0.10–0.34) based on │
│                          │ innovation activity.                                                                      │
│                          │ - Requires two consistent samples for ordinary reversals, while allowing a strong,        │
│                          │ slope-supported turn to pass immediately.                                                 │
│                          │ - Holds the previous output during unconfirmed opposite-direction moves, directly         │
│                          │ reducing spurious directional reversals without introducing centered-filter phase delay.  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
