│ patch_description        │ Add a lightweight 5–7 sample endpoint slope that acts only as an internal confidence      │
│                          │ signal for the alpha-beta tracker. The full and recent robust fits remain the sole        │
│                          │ reported-measurement path, preserving their strong tracking accuracy and noise reduction. │
│                          │ When the newest micro-scale slope agrees with the established recent/full/tracker         │
│                          │ direction, the filter modestly lowers velocity persistence and raises position gain for   │
│                          │ reduced lag. When it disagrees, it increases persistence and lowers alpha, preventing a   │
│                          │ few newest samples from inducing a false reversal. This supplies an additional temporal   │
│                          │ agreement test without introducing a third expensive robust regression.                   │
