│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the high tracking accuracy and low lag of the quadratic endpoint  │
│                          │ regression approach with the multi-scale trend-consistency and persistence gating from    │
│                          │ the smoother implementations.                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The enhanced filter uses a robust recency-weighted quadratic endpoint estimate, allowing  │
│                          │ curvature near genuine turning points without trailing-average lag. A recent linear slope │
│                          │ and full-window quadratic slope are compared to distinguish coherent trend changes from   │
│                          │ noisy local fluctuations. The alpha-beta tracker uses adaptive, innovation-bounded gains, │
│                          │ while a two-sample reversal confirmation gate suppresses isolated directional flips.      │
│                          │ Unlike a fully monotonic presentation layer, the output remains state-based so genuine    │
│                          │ dynamics are not flattened or held stale through valid turns.                             │
