│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_hysteretic_multiscale                                                            │
│ patch_description        │ The current approach uses two robust exponentially weighted endpoint regressions, a fixed │
│                          │ short-model ratio (0.52), blend weights of 0.34–0.70, a 0.12 slope prediction correction, │
│                          │ and symmetric hysteresis with a deadband of `max(0.11 * local_scale, 0.018 *              │
│                          │ global_noise)`. Its low lag and high correlation are strong, but the symmetric threshold  │
│                          │ permits many noise-induced counter-trend movements, producing high slope-change and       │
│                          │ false-reversal counts.                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The revised algorithm retains causal robust endpoint regression but changes the           │
│                          │ configuration to a three-scale consensus model: fast, medium, and slow horizons. Fast     │
│                          │ estimates preserve responsiveness, while medium/slow agreement suppresses isolated        │
│                          │ excursions. It adds confidence-adaptive blending, slope reliability weighting, and        │
│                          │ direction-dependent hysteresis. New movement can begin with a relatively small deadband,  │
│                          │ but an opposing movement must exceed a substantially larger reversal deadband and receive │
│                          │ consecutive confirmation before a direction reversal is accepted. A small adaptive        │
│                          │ alpha-beta tracking stage further suppresses jitter while preserving endpoint alignment   │
│                          │ and low latency.                                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key new parameters include: fast/medium horizon ratios (`0.38`, `0.62`),                  │
│                          │ disagreement-dependent fast blend range (`0.24–0.66`), predictive correction (`0.09`),    │
│                          │ forward deadband (`0.075 * scale`), reversal deadband (`0.19 * scale`), reversal          │
│                          │ confirmation count (`2`), and adaptive tracker gains (`alpha 0.42–0.82`, beta             │
│                          │ `0.05–0.19`). These settings specifically target lower false reversals and slope changes  │
│                          │ without heavily increasing lag.                                                           │
