│ patch_name               │ gated_alphabeta_tracker                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ This design replaces endpoint-regression blending with a causal robust alpha-beta state   │
│                          │ tracker. It uses the sliding window primarily for local noise estimation and              │
│                          │ multi-horizon slope agreement, rather than repeatedly fitting complete signal levels.     │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The tracker predicts the next endpoint from its persistent level and velocity state, then │
│                          │ applies a robust, Huber-limited innovation update. A recent slope and a longer slope      │
│                          │ modulate only the internal alpha/beta gains: agreement increases responsiveness, while    │
│                          │ disagreement reduces velocity adaptation and prevents short-lived noise bursts from       │
│                          │ creating false reversals. Reversal confirmation additionally requires persistent opposing │
│                          │ slope evidence before weak opposite innovations can overturn an established trend.        │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This preserves endpoint alignment and API compatibility, while targeting lower reversal   │
│                          │ counts, reduced noise sensitivity, and low-lag trend tracking.                            │
