                        Patch Metadata - Gen 47/100 - Novelty: 1/3 - Resample: 1/3 - Patch: 1/3                         
╭──────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ evidence_locked_tracker                                                                   │
│ patch_description        │ The current implementation obtains very low false reversals and slope changes through a   │
│                          │ hard output lock, but its `pending_count >= 2` gate and near-frozen counter-trend slope   │
│                          │ cause excessive lag (`0.97`) and poor tracking accuracy/correlation (`0.49`). The new     │
│                          │ configuration keeps a monotonic reported-output lock but lets the internal alpha-beta     │
│                          │ state adapt during pending turns.                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Key changes:                                                                              │
│                          │ - Replaces binary reversal counting with normalized cumulative counter-trend evidence     │
│                          │ (`turn_confirm=2.8`) plus a three-sample fallback.                                        │
│                          │ - Uses robust multi-scale endpoint regression: a longer weighted fit for stable level     │
│                          │ estimation and a shorter fit for responsive turn evidence.                                │
│                          │ - Uses stronger adaptive position gains (`alpha=0.20..0.58`) and slope tracking gains     │
│                          │ (`beta=0.08..0.30`) to reduce lag.                                                        │
│                          │ - Uses innovation clipping at `3.2 * noise_scale` for spike resistance.                   │
