│                          │ genuine curved turns, while a Huber reweighting pass limits impulse and outlier           │
│                          │ influence.                                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The tracker uses separate thresholds for ordinary direction maintenance and counter-trend │
│                          │ entry. Established trends require stronger, persistent opposing slope evidence before     │
│                          │ velocity is allowed to reverse. The reversal threshold is additionally increased as a     │
│                          │ trend matures, reducing short noise-driven reversals without preventing confirmed         │
│                          │ sustained turns. Adaptive gains remain responsive during coherent movement while using    │
│                          │ lower gains in quiet, noisy regions.                                                      │
