│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ bounded_reversal_catchup                                                                  │
│ patch_description        │ Add a short bounded catch-up mode when the persistent direction gate confirms a genuine   │
│                          │ reversal. The current presentation layer switches directly from `max` to `min` (or vice   │
│                          │ versa), which can expose a large jump from the internally tracked level and harm          │
│                          │ smoothness. Conversely, retaining the old level too long creates the measured post-turn   │
│                          │ lag.                                                                                      │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The new state releases the reported level toward the already-adapted internal level over  │
│                          │ three samples, with each movement capped relative to the robust noise scale. The final    │
│                          │ monotonic constraint is retained, so the output remains direction-safe and resistant to   │
│                          │ false reversals. This targets the weak lag/accuracy metrics without removing the source   │
│                          │ of the strong smoothness and false-reversal scores.                                       │
