│ patch_description        │ Replace the single-sample reversal threshold with cumulative, normalized multi-scale      │
│                          │ evidence and apply the directional lock to the reported output rather than freezing the   │
│                          │ internal alpha-beta state.                                                                │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The current tracker updates `previous_direction` as soon as velocity crosses its small    │
│                          │ deadband, which explains the very high slope-change and false-reversal counts despite     │
│                          │ excellent lag and point accuracy. The new gate requires counter-trend velocity,           │
│                          │ recent-slope confirmation, and a significant innovation in the same direction. Evidence   │
│                          │ accumulates for sustained turns, decays quickly for incoherent pullbacks, and confirms    │
│                          │ after sufficient normalized evidence or three coherent samples. Meanwhile, the internal   │
│                          │ position and velocity continue adapting, so the output can be released directly to the    │
│                          │ already-updated internal state once a genuine reversal is confirmed. This targets the     │
│                          │ dominant false-reversal penalty while retaining a bounded turn latency.                   │
