│ patch_name               │ evidence_weighted_turn_gate                                                               │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the binary consecutive-window reversal counter with normalized cumulative         │
│                          │ counter-trend evidence. The existing gate treats every qualifying counter-trend sample    │
│                          │ equally, so two weak movements can reverse the visible trend while a strong, coherent     │
│                          │ turn is delayed unless it passes the separate strong-move condition. Accumulating         │
│                          │ scale-normalized displacement evidence makes the decision robust to alternating           │
│                          │ low-amplitude noise, directly reducing false reversals and slope changes.                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The hard output lock is retained while a turn is pending, preserving smoothness. Evidence │
│                          │ is accumulated only when the proposed visible displacement, fused slope, and recent slope │
│                          │ are directionally consistent. A confirmed multi-scale turn therefore remains responsive,  │
│                          │ while weak or disagreement-driven pullbacks decay rather than becoming reversals.         │
