│ patch_name               │ evidence_locked_reversals                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the one-sample, innovation-only reversal test with a normalized cumulative        │
│                          │ counter-trend evidence gate. The existing tracker permits noisy velocity sign flips       │
│                          │ whenever the candidate velocity crosses zero with an innovation above a threshold,        │
│                          │ producing excessive slope changes and false reversals. The new gate retains the prior     │
│                          │ velocity direction as a hard output lock while an opposite turn is pending. Evidence is   │
│                          │ accumulated only when the fitted local slope, bounded innovation, and candidate velocity  │
│                          │ all agree on the counter-trend direction. Thus, alternating noise pullbacks reset/decay   │
│                          │ evidence, whereas a real sustained reversal is accepted after approximately 2.8           │
│                          │ normalized noise units or three coherent samples. A sufficiently strong, coherent turn    │
│                          │ remains fast-path eligible, protecting lag and responsiveness. This directly targets the  │
│                          │ poor smoothness and false-reversal metrics without requiring expensive multi-scale        │
│                          │ processing.                                                                               │
