│ patch_description        │ Strengthen the reported-output reversal gate using signed, innovation-normalized evidence │
│                          │ rather than treating every candidate displacement as equally valid evidence. A genuine    │
│                          │ reversal should have the candidate displacement and the clipped Kalman innovation         │
│                          │ pointing in the same direction across several causal updates. Noise-induced reversals     │
│                          │ frequently produce weak or inconsistent innovations, so they no longer accumulate         │
│                          │ confirmation score merely because the internally predicted state moved slightly across    │
│                          │ the reported level.                                                                       │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The gate retains an immediate-turn path for unusually large coherent moves to preserve    │
│                          │ responsiveness, while ordinary turns require three qualifying samples and cumulative      │
│                          │ normalized innovation evidence. This directly targets the remaining false reversals and   │
│                          │ excess slope changes without changing the endpoint estimator or Kalman state model.       │
